      "receiptId": "mulled-ale.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Modern domestic cookery, and useful receipt book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Elizabeth Hammond (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#hammond-1819\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EHammond 1819\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EMulled ale.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nBoil a quart of good ale with some nutmegs beat up six eggs, and mix them with a little cold ale then pour the hot ale to it, and return it several times to prevent it from curdling \u0027till warm, and stir it till sufficiently thick, add a piece of butter or a glass of brandy, and serve it with dry toast.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
